 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Sure, see as ver and star as estrella. Ver means to see, and estrella means star. Precisely. How about, I want go out tonight, see a movie or eat at a nice restaurant? Ver means to see, so you' say ver cine if you want go see a movie. Then you' say estrella because home means casa. So it would be estrella casa. That's a bit of a catch all. Soy means I am, so with sir it sounds formal. You' use it with people you don't know well. I' glad I could clear it up. Spanish conjugations look complicated, but they follow patterns. Keep practicing, and you'll have it down in no time.",
